From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/meson: crtc: put dv_debug property blob reference

meson_crtc_atomic_set_property() looks the dv_debug blob up with
drm_property_lookup_blob(), which returns a reference the caller must
drop with drm_property_blob_put(). The dv_debug branch never does, on
either exit: it returns 0 after the kmalloc failure and again after
copying the string out. The reference DRM core takes for the property
value is a separate, balanced one.

The property is attached to every CRTC with no SoC condition. Kodi hits
it routinely - AMLCodec sets enable_fel/enable_mel on open and
enable_fel 0, enable_mel 0 and force_unmap on close, one fresh blob per
call - so each call strands a blob plus its data for the life of the
device. A few dozen bytes a few times per playback: slow growth, no
corruption, no crash.

Drop the reference on both paths; blob->data is only read by the memcpy
that precedes the put. Not compiled or run here.
--- a/drivers/drm/meson_crtc.c
+++ b/drivers/drm/meson_crtc.c
@@ -437,11 +437,14 @@
 
 		/* blob->data is not null‑terminated */
 		str = kmalloc(blob->length + 1, GFP_KERNEL);
-		if (!str)
+		if (!str) {
+			drm_property_blob_put(blob);
 			return 0;
+		}
 
 		memcpy(str, blob->data, blob->length);
 		str[blob->length] = '\0';
+		drm_property_blob_put(blob);
 		amdv_debug_store(str);
 
 		kfree(str);
